From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:19:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/dovi_reshape: add a Dolby Vision RPU reshaping
 helper

Dolby Vision profile 5 carries IPTPQc2 in its base layer and needs the
per-frame RPU reshaping curves before any tone mapper can use it. Only
vf_libplacebo applies them today, so every other tone-mapping path in
libavfilter (zscale + tonemap, tonemap_opencl, tonemap_vaapi) shows the
base layer with wrong colours.

Add one internal helper that the filters can share: it validates the
RPU, evaluates the polynomial and MMR curves per component, and decodes
the reshaped signal to PQ BT.2020 RGB through the RPU's matrices. The
steps follow libplacebo v7.360.1 (pl_shader_dovi_reshape and
pl_shader_decode_color in src/shaders/colorspace.c, pl_map_dovi_metadata),
whose notice the file carries. Streams with a
residual enhancement layer (profile 7) are refused.

The unit test builds RPUs with known curves and checks the helper
against values from a separate double-precision model, including the
pivot boundary, a planted wrong MMR coefficient, and the refusals.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
